  "id": "Wandsworth-2026_0196",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "Installation of 1No. BT Street Hub Unit and associated illuminated digital advertisement panels on either side of the unit. ",
  "development_type": "Other advertisements",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed Street Hub, by reason of its scale, design and location would fail to minimise street clutter, result in loss of public open space and harm to the character and appearance of the local area, including the setting of adjacent heritage asset. Furthermore, the hub would create an unnecessary obstruction of the public space, hindering the convenient and safe passage of pedestrians and increases potential distraction to drivers. Whilst the proposal would result in some facilities for the general public, these benefits are low and do not outweigh the harm identified. The proposal therefore fails to comply with the Town and Country Planning (Control of Advertisements) (England) Regulations 2007, National Planning Policy Framework (2024), D3, D8, HC1, T2 and T4 of the London Plan (2021), policies LP1, LP3, LP9, LP22 and LP50 of the Local Plan (2023).",
    "Reason : 2 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to make available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the principle of the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal."
  ],
